#
# /etc/rc -- Renux system startup script.
#
# Like the BSD rc files, this runs once the root filesystem is up. It performs
# the actions this system actually supports and records them in the system log;
# there are no placeholders for services that do not exist.

# Each rc.d script announces itself the way FreeBSD's rc.subr does
# ("Starting syslogd."), so the console shows one line per service.
/etc/rc.d/syslogd

logger rc: multi-user startup
